invariant: INV-16
file: src/sha3.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha3-bmi
reason: sha3_on_instructions picks sha3_hw.c's x86-64 copy where the
  session's ch_cfg.cpu holds CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX alone, so a session whose
  caller never said the CPU has BMI1 runs ANDN, and dies of SIGILL on a
  CPU without it. Every digest is still right on a CPU with it. The qemu
  lane's sha3-bmi part counts the SHA-3 calls under each value, and runs
  ML-DSA-87's vectors under CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX alone on a model without BMI1,
  where they must pass. x86-64 alone compiles this arm of sha3.h.

--- old
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_BMI1 | CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX;
--- new
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX;
